%
% confidence ≠ probability guard (#506 AC-2; red if violated).
% diagnosis(patient, flu) is an asserted fact (in input.nq) carrying confidence
% 0.9. Under ProbabilisticProfile with a declared model, its marginal MUST be 1.0
% — confidence is metadata, NEVER a probability. A binding probability of 0.9
% would mean confidence leaked into the probability model: the failure mode this
% case exists to catch.
% Expected: X = ex:flu with probability 1.0 (NOT 0.9), status ok.
:- prefix(ex, 'https://example.org/profiles/probabilistic-confidence-guard/').
:- probability_model(full_independence).
:- confidence(ex:diagnosis(ex:patient, ex:flu), 0.9).
?- ex:diagnosis(ex:patient, X).
